      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>If \\( f(x)=2x+3 \\), find \\( f^{-1}(x) \\).</p>\\[ f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-3}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.B — Composite and inverse",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Given \\(f(x)=2x+3\\) and \\(g(x)=x^{2}\\), find (a) \\(fg(3)\\), (b) \\(f^{-1}(x)\\).</p><p>(a) \\(fg(3)=f(9)=2(9)+3=21\\).</p><p>(b) Let \\(y=2x+3\\). Swap and solve: \\(x=\\dfrac{y-3}{2}\\). So \\(f^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{x-3}{2}\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example D — Algebraic Structure & Vieta's Root Relations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 10x + 25 = 0 \\) and verify the sum and product of its roots.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>Factor into binomials: \\( (x - 5)(x - 5) = 0 \\implies x = 5 \\text{ or } x = 5 \\).</li><li>Check Vieta's formulas: sum \\( = 5 + 5 = \\mathbf{10} \\) and product \\( = (5)(5) = \\mathbf{25} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "\\(h(x)=\\dfrac{3x-1}{2}\\). Find \\(h^{-1}(4)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(y=\\dfrac{3x-1}{2}\\Rightarrow2y=3x-1\\Rightarrow x=\\dfrac{2y+1}{3}\\). So \\(h^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{2x+1}{3}\\) and \\(h^{-1}(4)=\\dfrac{9}{3}=3\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "fn": "2*x + 3",
          "xrange": [
            -4,
            4
          ],
          "yrange": [
            -5,
            9
